        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "Add grouped Claw schema and read-only add plan",
        "body": "## Summary\n\nImplements the first read-only slice of RFC 0016 behind the process-only experimental gate:\n\n- Strict grouped schema version `1` with `agent`, `workspace`, `packages`, `mcpServers`, and `cronJobs` ownership boundaries.\n- One-Claw/one-agent planning: every add creates a new `agents.list[]` entry and a new workspace; agent or workspace collisions block instead of merging.\n- Package identity and version come from `package.json` plus `openclaw.claw`; standalone manifests receive an explicit development identity and digest.\n- Only portable agent settings are accepted. Models, providers, auth, bindings, runtimes, `agent.skills`, connectors, optional/`required` components, unknown fields, resolved MCP secrets, and floating package versions fail closed.\n- `openclaw claws inspect <source>` and `openclaw claws add <source> --dry-run --json`; the prototype `apply` and feed CLI surfaces are removed.\n- Complete add plans include the generated agent config, workspace creation and file digests, skill/plugin packages, top-level MCP declarations, and cron jobs pinned to the final local agent id.\n- Existing agent, configured/existing workspace, MCP server, and persisted cron id collisions produce stable blockers.\n- Workspace sources are package-confined regular files with symlink, hardlink, traversal, and size checks.\n\nWhen `OPENCLAW_EXPERIMENTAL_CLAWS=1` is absent, the `claws` command remains unregistered and absent from help/completion. Machine-readable results are versioned and include `stability: \"experimental\"`.\n\nThis PR does not mutate config, create workspaces, install packages, configure MCP, create cron jobs, or persist provenance.\n\n## RFC\n\nTracks https://github.com/openclaw/rfcs/pull/27 at RFC head `5829ce30c1520e46d21f291d39866d2cb25d1d14`.\n\n## Validation\n\nBranch head: `7f3bab34903639a51545291b6c2286c678695364`\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs \\\n  src/claws/schema.test.ts src/claws/feed.test.ts src/claws/experimental.test.ts \\\n  src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts src/cli/program/command-registry.test.ts \\\n  src/cli/program/root-command-descriptions.test.ts src/cli/argv.test.ts \\\n  src/claws/lifecycle.e2e.test.ts\n# 186 tests passed across 4 Vitest shards\n\npnpm exec oxlint src/claws src/cli/claws-cli.ts \\\n  src/cli/claws-cli.runtime.ts src/cli/claws-cli.test.ts\n# 0 warnings, 0 errors\n\ngit diff --check\nnode scripts/check-no-conflict-markers.mjs\n# passed\n```\n\nReal CLI proof produced `openclaw.clawAddPlan.v1`, `stability: \"experimental\"`, one generated agent config, eight actions, and zero blockers. Root help contained zero `claws` entries with the gate unset and one with it enabled.\n\n`pnpm exec tsgo --noEmit --pretty false` reaches only the pre-existing unrelated `src/secrets/config-io.ts` TS4058 (`configWritePostCommitRollback`).\n",
